  "meta": {
    "document": "San Francisco Adopted Budget FY2026-27",
    "title": "San Francisco — the money trail",
    "grand_total": 16851826113,
    "year": 2027,
    "note": "San Francisco is a consolidated city-and-county — one government, one budget, no separate county line. This is the adopted all-funds budget for FY2026-27 (the fiscal year beginning July 1, 2026), $16.85 billion, shown by department. The General Fund is about $6.18 billion of it; the rest is largely self-supporting enterprises — the Airport, the Public Utilities Commission, Muni, and the Port — that fund themselves from their own revenue. Every figure traces to the Controller’s machine-readable Annual Appropriation Ordinance dataset on DataSF."
  },
